[["Map",1,2,72,73],"blog",["Map",3,4,15,16,25,26,35,36,45,46,54,55,63,64],"bank2curb",{"id":3,"data":5,"body":11,"filePath":12,"digest":13,"deferredRender":14},{"title":6,"description":7,"buildDate":8,"pubDate":9,"updatedDate":10},"Bank 2 Curb","Journal entry",["Date","2025-08-23T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-17T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"import ImageLightBox from \"../../components/ImageLightBox.astro\";\n\n\u003Cdiv id=\"blog_content\">\n    \n    \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n    \n        \u003Ch2 class=\"subheader\">{`\n            August Bank Holiday Weekend\n        `}\u003C/h2>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/form_sketch.jpeg\" gallery=\"tetris\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/backfill_sketch2.jpeg\" gallery=\"tetris\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/backfill_sketch.jpeg\" gallery=\"tetris\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I set myself the challenge of concreting two obstacles over the Saturday and most of Sunday with backfill preparations made throughout the week. Although I succeeded, ultimately I overstretched myself and Sunday’s concrete suffered.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The design for the bank2curb must have come from Dan Mirza’s repeatedly requesting a “slope/incline” to decked curb combined with inspiration from Paul Carroll bank to curb obstacle at his new spot.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The curb stones already existed at Brickside and just needed transporting. I can’t say for sure how much each one weighs but I managed to get 3 in my the back of the Seat Ibiza without crushing any part of myself and doing limited damage to the car which made me feel like a world’s strongest man contestant.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/curbs_car.jpeg\" />\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            At one point when unloading at the other end, I almost tripped backwards with a curb stone leaning against me which would have been a very bad outcome if it had fallen on me.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I had done a mock up of the backfill cross section at brickside to calculate how many red bricks I would need. That came to about 160.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/tetris.jpeg\" gallery=\"tetris\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/tetris3.jpeg\" gallery=\"tetris\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            There was a pile of cleaned bricks at Brickside and one load in my car is about 60 bricks, so that means putting 15-20 in a wheelbarrow/on a skateboard, rolling them to the car, stacking them in the boot, driving 5mins up the river, unloading them onto the skateboard and rolling them up the lane to their next resting place.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/bricks_curbs.jpeg\" gallery=\"materials\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/bricks_curbs2.jpeg\" gallery=\"materials\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Ch2>23rd August\u003C/h2>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            First job was to establish the foundation. This meant laying a row of 26 red bricks side by side on a bed of ballast and cement mix to try to prevent any movement over time. Then went on the curb stones lined up at the edge of the row of bricks, leaving 10mm between the curbs to fill with a poly resin? later.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/foundations.jpeg\" gallery=\"foundations\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/foundations2.jpeg\" gallery=\"foundations\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            Behind the first row of bricks was placed another lengthways row of bricks that would support the next level of backfill bricks. This layer was laid side by side on their sides, requiring about 39 bricks to bring the level up high enough. For the deck/back section, the total red bricks needed to accommodate the 3 curb stones came to 78.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            By noon I had the shuttering in place to contain the deck and make for easy screeding and levelling. In the recess I placed a variety of rocks and loose render that had fallen from the walls at the spot, and then on top of that I laid a section of heras fence as rebar.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/deck_backfill.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/deck_backfill2.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I imagine I went home for lunch at that point and after my return for the afternoon shift, I had the concrete deck in and level by 3pm.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/deck_conned_top.jpeg\" />\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I pressed on into the afternoon, laying out the remaining red bricks for the bank backfill, then adding the stones and rubble for in between the gaps, got the heras fence rebar ready and chipped out the tarmac to create a lip for the bank transition.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/bank_backfill.jpeg\" />\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The sound of me chiselling into the floor attracted the attention of workers from the reclaimed brick yard on the other side of the wall and they came to see what I was up to and essentially gave me their blessing to carry on.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            Carry on I did and by 8pm the bank was in and had been seen to by the finishing trowel. It been a 12 hour day with 0 assistance other than some passing moral support.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/all_con_right.jpeg\" gallery=\"conned\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/all_con_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"conned\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The build had been successful but I knew I had much more to come the following day and I was quite unprepared.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/next_right.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/next_centre.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/next_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/dry_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"dry\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_main/dry_left_low.jpeg\" gallery=\"dry\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003C/div>\n\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/bank2curb.mdx","831fa96b3537773f",true,"bank2curb_wings",{"id":15,"data":17,"body":22,"filePath":23,"digest":24,"deferredRender":14},{"title":18,"description":7,"buildDate":19,"pubDate":20,"updatedDate":21},"Bank 2 Curb Wings",["Date","2025-08-28T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"import ImageLightBox from \"../../components/ImageLightBox.astro\";\n\n\u003Cdiv id=\"blog_content\">\n    \n    \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n        \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/wing_sketch.jpeg\" gallery=\"sketch\" />\n        \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/wing_sketch2.jpeg\" gallery=\"sketch\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/leftwing_backfill.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/rightwing_backfill2.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal_ima÷ge\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_wings/leftwing_backfill2.jpeg\" gallery=\"\" /> */}\n            {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/rightwing_backfill.jpeg\" gallery=\"\" /> */}\n            {/* \u003Cimg class=\"journal÷_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/bank2curb_wings/leftwing_backfill3.jpeg\" gallery=\"\" /> */}\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            Although the curbs, deck and bank were set and curing nicely through the late summer days, the obstacle was not finished. To be able to take advantage of 100% of the grindable curb space, wings would be required and I hardly delayed in getting them in.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/leftwing_backfill4.jpeg\" gallery=\"soil\" /> */}\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/backfill_soil_right.jpeg\" gallery=\"soil\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/backfill_soil_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"soil\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            Wednesday 27th, I had the shuttering figured out and the backfill and heras rebar prepared. Thursday 28th after work, I was ready to go and managed to get a hand from Yangchen, who exchanged his help for an interview for his dissertation.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/yang_shov.jpeg\" gallery=\"yang\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/yang_shov2.jpeg\" gallery=\"yang\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            We were concreting at 7.30 and since the right wing went in quickly and Yangchen was down for more we pressed on and got the left wing done on the same night, finishing around 10.30.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/yang_wing.jpeg\" gallery=\"yang-finish\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/yang_wing2.jpeg\" gallery=\"yang-finish\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/yang_wing3.jpeg\" gallery=\"yang-finish\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/yang2.jpeg\" gallery=\"name\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/yang3.jpeg\" gallery=\"name\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I hadn’t made up my mind whether to make the wings into a roll on grind but Yangchen wanted it so I went with it and was pleased with the result so I asked him to write the Chinese characters of his name on the roll on grind as a momento.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/next_wings.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/next_wings_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/next_wings2.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n\n        \u003Ch2>Reflections\u003C/h2>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/lacquered.jpeg\" gallery=\"finish\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/bank2curb_wings/dried.jpeg\" gallery=\"finish\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003C/div>\n\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/bank2curb_wings.mdx","5e87ca66b93299aa","day1",{"id":25,"data":27,"body":32,"filePath":33,"digest":34,"deferredRender":14},{"title":28,"description":7,"buildDate":29,"pubDate":30,"updatedDate":31},"First Build",["Date","2025-08-16T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-15T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"import ImageLightBox from \"../../components/ImageLightBox.astro\";\n\n\u003Cdiv id=\"blog_content\">\n    \n    \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n        \n        \u003Ch2 class=\"subheader\">{`\n          Day 1 - August 16th 2025\n        `}\u003C/h2>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The desperate burst of effort at Otherside was doomed to be a deadend. I had planned to start building there on Saturday but on Thursday night I had noticed signs of the inevitable. With no intention to put money into a lost cause, I moped for the morning wondering what to do and eventually decided to scope out a pedestrianised road 1/2 a mile up river that I'd heard Pat mention in the past.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_build/firstday_road.jpeg\" />\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I went down for a reccy, saw the existing retaining wall and the soft tarmac and the road barrier already down there asking to be backfill and decided to send it. I hauled 75 red bricks from Brickside in my car and set up the formers.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_noforms.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill1\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_bricks.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill1\" />\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            There were plentiful rocks and hardcore for the small back fill. I had a wire net and some leftover heras fence for rebar.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_right.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill2\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_close.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill2\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill2\" />\n\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            By 6.30pm I had the materials for concrete, water and a shovel and began mixing up on the tarmac.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/backfill/backfill_rebar.jpeg\" />\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            By 8.30pm the shaping was done. 2x ballast2:sharp1:0.5cement mixes and 1x sharp1:10mmgravel1:0.5cement mixes. The ballast mix for the body and the gravel for the coping and the transition. The tarmac already had a lip so there was no need to chip out a recess for the transition concrete.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_right_medium2.jpeg\" gallery=\"conFinish\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_face.jpeg\" gallery=\"conFinish\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"conFinish\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_right_medium.jpeg\" gallery=\"conFinish\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/con_left_high.jpeg\" gallery=\"conFinish\" />\n\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The coping was shaped with a tool made from a cyclindrical water bottle screwed to a bit of batten for a handle. I'd first used this improvised coping tool on the big QP at Brickside. Although it served me well, its fundamental flaw was its flimsiness and the fact I was afraid it might break mid-build.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n        \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/conned/coping_left_dark.jpeg\" />\n\n        \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The concrete had gone in well and no one who passed by had been offended by me building.\u003Cbr>\u003C/br>The spot was a goer.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n\n        \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_right2.jpeg\" gallery=\"nextDay\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_front_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"nextDay\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"nextDay\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/coping_next_right.jpeg\" gallery=\"nextDay\" />\n            \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/coping_next_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"nextDay\" />\n            {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_front.jpeg\" /> */}\n            {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_right.jpeg\" /> */}\n\n        \u003C/div>\n\n        \u003Cimg class=\"landscape_image\" src=\"../../../public/images/first_build/nextday/con_next_far_left.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/day1.mdx","ff46a7ac81ccb6da","expansion2",{"id":35,"data":37,"body":42,"filePath":43,"digest":44,"deferredRender":14},{"title":38,"description":7,"buildDate":39,"pubDate":40,"updatedDate":41},"Conny QP Extension",["Date","2025-08-24T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-16T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"import ImageLightBox from \"../../components/ImageLightBox.astro\";\n\n\u003Cdiv id=\"blog_content\">\n  \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            On Monday evening I reclaimed two more road barriers and the following evening hauled 110 red bricks from the Otherside piles.    \n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/backfill/backfill_bricks5.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/backfill/backfill_bricks3.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/backfill/backfill_bricks4.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Ch2 class=\"subheader\">August 24th\u003C/h2>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            To my demise, that afternoon I was driving to Halifax for a gig and was not even backfill ready at 10.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox\n      src=\"/images/conxtension/backfill/backfill_rocks.jpeg\" gallery=\"\"\n    />\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            With great solo effort, by 3pm the concrete was sufficiently shaped and finished. The coping is wonky because of my flimsy not fit for purpose coping shaping tool. And the deck is proud on the right side because I ran out of time. But it would go.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/con/con_right.jpeg\" gallery=\"conxtension\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/con/con_right_low.jpeg\" gallery=\"conxtension\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/con/con_coping_right.jpeg\" gallery=\"conxtension\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/con/con_left_full.jpeg\" gallery=\"conxtension\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/con/con_coping_left.jpeg\" gallery=\"conxtension\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/con/con_coping_left_close.jpeg\" gallery=\"conxtension\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/con/con_front.jpeg\" gallery=\"conxtension\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            I made the bold choice to leave the qp uncovered mid afternoon of bank holiday Monday and within 2 hours someone who'd gone to inspect the spot themselves sent me a photo of a strange racist message written by finger in the concrete. When I returned from the gig that night I stopped by to check for more damage and had to patch some tags scratched into the both sides of the face. It would take a few more attacks before I never left any fresh concrete uncovered.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/next/next_right.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/next/next_face.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/next/next_left_wide.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/next/next_coping_right.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/conxtension/next/next_left_full.jpeg\" gallery=\"next\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n            The coping is wobbly as anything but and the right side of the face is a bit lumpy but a week before there wasn't a whippy quarter pipe in Sheffield and now there was.\n        `}\u003C/p>\n\n  \u003C/div>\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/expansion2.mdx","56ab14391703178c","first_sesh",{"id":45,"data":47,"body":51,"filePath":52,"digest":53,"deferredRender":14},{"title":48,"description":7,"buildDate":49,"pubDate":50},"First Session",["Date","2025-09-07T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-06-19T00:00:00.000Z"],"import ImageLightBox from \"../../components/ImageLightBox.astro\";\n\n\u003Cdiv id=\"blog_content\">\n    \n  \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n      Return of the bricks\n     `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ed_50.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ed_502.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ed_close.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ed_close2.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/jen_carve.jpg\" />\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/john_smith.jpg\" />\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/max_fscrook.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/max_fscrook2.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/max_fscrook3.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/max_nosegrind.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/mike_502.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/mike_crook.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/mike_lip.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/mike_lip2.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/mike_tail.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/choms/welsh_lads.jpg\" />\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ste_hurricane.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ste_hurricane2.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ste_hurricane3.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ste_nose.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ste_nose2.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/ste_sugarcane.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/ste_push.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/wannop_fscrook.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/wannop_fscrook2.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/bank2curb/wannop_wax.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/choms/choms.jpg\" />\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/choms/ledge_seat2.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/choms/ledge_seat3.jpg\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/choms/ledge_seat.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/choms/ledge_seat4.jpg\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/choms/alley.jpg\" />\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/luke_5.0.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/luke_nosegrind2.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/max_crook.jpg\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/luke_nose.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/mike_5.0.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/mike_50.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/max_crook2.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/mike_5.02.jpg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/mike_floor.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/qp_vibe.jpg\" />\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/first_sesh/qp/ste_5.0.jpg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n  \u003C/div>\n\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/first_sesh.mdx","76c79720b84d52ff","low_qp",{"id":54,"data":56,"body":60,"filePath":61,"digest":62,"deferredRender":14},{"title":57,"description":7,"buildDate":58,"pubDate":59},"Low Brick QP",["Date","2025-08-30T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"],"import ImageLightBox from \"../../components/ImageLightBox.astro\";\n\n\u003Cdiv id=\"blog_content\">\n    \n  \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n      Return of the bricks\n     `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/backfill/backfill_far.jpeg\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/backfill/backfill_right.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/backfill/backfill_left.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/backfill/small_fill.jpeg\" />\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/backfill/small_filL_right.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/backfill/small_fill_left.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/sec_brix_prep.jpeg\" />\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/first_brix_right.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/first_brix.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/first_brix_left.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/face_brix.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/face_brix_right.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/deck_mix.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/deck_mix2.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/brix.jpeg\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/brix_done2.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/brix_done_close.jpeg\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/brix_done_far.jpeg\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/brix_fresh_right.jpeg\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/brix_done_left.jpeg\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/brix/brix_dark.jpeg\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/coping_form.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/coping_tool.jpeg\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/coping_tool2.jpeg\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/coping_tool3.jpeg\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/coping_shaped2.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/coping_shaped.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/coping_shaped3.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/cement_price.jpeg\" /> */}\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/trans_shaped.jpeg\" />\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_right3.jpeg\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_right4.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_coping.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_left2.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_left3.jpeg\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_left5.jpeg\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_front.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_front2.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_front_far.jpeg\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_right5.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_right6.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_right8.jpeg\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_right2.jpeg\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_right7.jpeg\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_right9.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_front3.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_left4.jpeg\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_left.jpeg\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_left_far.jpeg\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/conned_right.jpeg\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/coping_close.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/low_qp/concreting/cured.jpeg\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n  \u003C/div>\n\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/low_qp.mdx","f5b3891eda6ac35c","rods_curb",{"id":63,"data":65,"body":69,"filePath":70,"digest":71,"deferredRender":14},{"title":66,"description":7,"buildDate":67,"pubDate":68},"Rod's Revenge",["Date","2026-06-21T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-08-29T00:00:00.000Z"],"import ImageLightBox from \"../../components/ImageLightBox.astro\";\n\n\u003Cdiv id=\"blog_content\">\n    \n  \u003Cdiv class=\"image_cont\">\n\n    \u003Ch2 class=\"subheader\">{`\n      The Lower Rods Curb Reborn\n    `}\u003C/h2>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Every DIY needs a good curb. Mikeside had been blessed early on with a 2.5m curb from the NSD factory, but as the spot matured there was an obvious need for a longer one.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    A curb that had been poured in place at Lower Rods in Leeds (RIP) was universally praised among the Sheff scene and the dimensions even shared in the main group chat in hopes that it could be recreated.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/spec.jpeg\"/>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/wholepark_before.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    At the time, after an intense 8 months of building at the spot, I was trying to force myself to not build anything but couldn’t resist casually reaching out to the original creator, Chris Parsons, just to ask for more details about the recipe he used for future reference. Not only was he forthcoming with advice but he immediately offered to come and help with the build whenever that might be.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Somewhat tentatively, I proposed a date for a Sunday a month in the future and continued to pester him with questions about the forms, the mix and the required tools.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    When it came to the date, we ended up delaying for a week as I’d naively assumed the forms could be quickly prepped but that was definitely not the case:\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    - Firstly I had to skate 3 3.5m lengths of thick timber by hand half a mile up the road from Wickes.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/timber.jpeg\" gallery=\"timber\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/timber2.jpeg\" gallery=\"timber\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    - Second, the 3 lengths of timber needed to be cut at a 67degree along their entire length. Me not having a circular saw, this is where Beeside’s Ashley saved the day.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/ash.jpeg\" gallery=\"cutting\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/end.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/end2.jpeg\" gallery=\"cutting\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/end3.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/end4.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`Ashley and co came over from Manchester for the day bringing his circular saw and 4 batteries with which we were able to cut 1 length and half of the other 2 before the batteries gave up.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    It was then left to me to finish the job with a hand saw (and chisel) after work during the week. This was a brutal slog that must’ve taken 2 hours, but it got done.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/timber_cut2.jpeg\"/>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Later with Tomasz’ screw gun, the forms were strapped together and the simple task of prepping the forms was done.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/forms_assembled.jpeg\" gallery=\"assembled\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/forms_assembled2.jpeg\" gallery=\"assembled\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    **** APRIL PAINTING ****\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/april.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/april2.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/form_painted2.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/april3.jpeg\" gallery=\"forms_painted\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/form/form_painted.jpeg\" gallery=\"forms_painted\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    The next Sunday came and a heatwave was in full swing. I started the morning with a trip to wickes for 14 bags of 40n blue circle premix that Chris had requested. Premix is spenny but should guarantee the strength and uniformity desired for a slappy that is certain to take a relentless battering for the duration of its existence.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/nsd_buildday.jpeg\" gallery=\"nsd_curbs\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/nsd_buildday2.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/nsdcurb.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/nsd_removed.jpeg\" gallery=\"nsd_curbs\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Chris, Ben and Jake arrived after 11am and immediately started preparing the rebar and rough cutting into the tarmac ground.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/rebar.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/rebar2.jpeg\" gallery=\"team_leeds\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/lamppost.jpeg\" gallery=\"team_leeds\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/floor_cut.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    We set up the 5.2m long forms using a string line and level to keep them as straight and flat as possible. 2 bridges were screw into the top and heavy weights placed along the outside to prevent the forms bowing.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Chris sealed the bottom edges of the forms with some hardening/expanding(?) foam and back(inner)fill was placed in the center.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/foaming2.jpeg\" />\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/lamppost2.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    By 1 the concrete was being mixed with a few extra people showing up and pitching in. The moist concrete was slopped in and forced as far down into the forms as possible with a short bit of batten and a thin metal bar for a PDT.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/mixing.jpeg\" gallery=\"mixing\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/precon/mixing2.jpeg\" gallery=\"mixing\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Within an hour, 13 bags had been mixed and the forms were full; the top screeded, worked and levelled off then the outside of the forms battered a little to try to make the outer concrete settle. Then it was left to sit and go off in the heat for a while.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/conned.jpeg\" gallery=\"conned\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/conned2.jpeg\" gallery=\"conned\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/conned3.jpeg\" gallery=\"conned\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    ****\n    (nb Chris’ reassuring presence and strong leadership presence had the affect of making me complacent and forgetting that i was meant to be in charge/responsible for the outcome which led to the ridge)\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    We got on with some skating and returned occasionally to work the top with the improvised wood trowel. Once again, I dropped the ball as project leader and let some significant ridges and dips appear around the bridges where it was harder to pass the trowel underneath it and achieve uniformity (fortunately this was ironed out at a later date).\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    After the concrete was starting to harden fully, Chris got out his 67 degree trowel and shaped the edges all the way along the top of the curb on both sides, then every hour or so for the rest of the day I stroked the top with a finishing trowel.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/finished.jpeg\" gallery=\"finished\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/finished2.jpeg\" gallery=\"finished\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/finished3.jpeg\" gallery=\"finished\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/finished4.jpeg\" gallery=\"finished\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/finished5.jpeg\" gallery=\"finished\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/finished6.jpeg\" gallery=\"finished\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Before leaving, I doused the whole thing in water and then laid a sheet of thick black plastic over it, donated by Chris, and secured it with heavy weights.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/wrapped.jpeg\" gallery=\"wrapped\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/wrapped2.jpeg\" gallery=\"wrapped\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/footsteps.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    For the next 2.5 weeks it would stay like this curing, only being uncovered to be watered when possible.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/watered.jpeg\" gallery=\"watered\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/concreting/watered2.jpeg\" gallery=\"watered\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    After a patient 3 week wait, Chris returned on a Wednesday evening with his hand held grinder and assortment of brushes.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/popped_forms.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/popped_forms2.jpeg\" gallery=\"popped\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/deformed2.jpeg\" gallery=\"popped\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/prepaint.jpeg\" gallery=\"popped\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/deformed1.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/deformed3.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/deformed4.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/prepaint2.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    We patched some spots with quick set concrete along the bottom edge of the curb where our poking and pushing hadn’t been thorough enough and the concrete hadn’t reached leaving unfortunate voids.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/holes.jpeg\" gallery=\"holes\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/hole.jpeg\" gallery=\"holes\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Meanwhile Chris got started with the diamond grinder disc, smoothing out the ridges and levelling the dips to achieve a more or less perfectly straight and flat top surface.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/smoothing.jpeg\" gallery=\"smoothing\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/smoothing2.jpeg\" gallery=\"smoothing\" />\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Once the curb had reached it final form, the disc was swapped for a finer grain and the buffing commenced, making the surface smooth to the point of shiny before finally a first layer of red masonry paint could go on.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/painting.jpeg\" gallery=\"painting\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/painting3.jpeg\" gallery=\"painting\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/painting4.jpeg\" gallery=\"painting\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/painting5.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/painting6.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    The second coat of paint and final layers of lacquer would go on the next evening and the curb was christened.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/painted2.jpeg\" />\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/painted.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/done_end2.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n    \u003Cdiv class=\"carousel\">\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/done_end.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/done_full.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n      \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/done_full2.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" />\n      {/* \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/painted/done_full3.jpeg\" gallery=\"backfill\" /> */}\n    \u003C/div>\n\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Thanks for everything, Chris. The curb would not be what it is without your guidance and graft. Sheffield and anyone else who comes to skate the spot is blessed.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    Also big up to Ashley, Ben, Jake, Joel for coming out of their way to help.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003Cp class=\"journal_entry\">{`\n    This has been a Lower Rods, Beeside, Mikeside production.\n    `}\u003C/p>\n\n    \u003CImageLightBox src=\"/images/rod_curb/postcon/wear.jpeg\"/>\n\n    \u003C/div>\n\n\u003C/div>","src/content/blog/rods_curb.mdx","4cf7d9ec0c685377","meta::meta",["Map",74,75,76,77,78,79],"astro-config-digest","{\"root\":{},\"srcDir\":{},\"publicDir\":{},\"outDir\":{},\"cacheDir\":{},\"site\":\"https://example.com\",\"compressHTML\":true,\"base\":\"/\",\"trailingSlash\":\"ignore\",\"output\":\"static\",\"scopedStyleStrategy\":\"attribute\",\"build\":{\"format\":\"directory\",\"client\":{},\"server\":{},\"assets\":\"_astro\",\"serverEntry\":\"entry.mjs\",\"redirects\":true,\"inlineStylesheets\":\"auto\",\"concurrency\":1},\"server\":{\"open\":false,\"host\":false,\"port\":4321,\"allowedHosts\":[]},\"redirects\":{},\"image\":{\"endpoint\":{\"route\":\"/_image\"},\"service\":{\"entrypoint\":\"astro/assets/services/sharp\",\"config\":{}},\"dangerouslyProcessSVG\":false,\"domains\":[],\"remotePatterns\":[],\"responsiveStyles\":false},\"devToolbar\":{\"enabled\":true},\"markdown\":{\"syntaxHighlight\":{\"type\":\"shiki\",\"excludeLangs\":[\"math\"]},\"shikiConfig\":{\"langs\":[],\"langAlias\":{},\"theme\":\"github-dark\",\"themes\":{},\"wrap\":false,\"transformers\":[]},\"remarkPlugins\":[],\"rehypePlugins\":[],\"remarkRehype\":{},\"processor\":{\"name\":\"unified\",\"options\":{\"remarkPlugins\":[],\"rehypePlugins\":[],\"remarkRehype\":{}}}},\"security\":{\"checkOrigin\":true,\"allowedDomains\":[],\"csp\":false,\"actionBodySizeLimit\":1048576,\"serverIslandBodySizeLimit\":1048576},\"env\":{\"schema\":{},\"validateSecrets\":false},\"prerenderConflictBehavior\":\"warn\",\"fonts\":[{\"name\":\"Atkinson\",\"cssVariable\":\"--font-atkinson\",\"provider\":{\"name\":\"local\"},\"fallbacks\":[\"sans-serif\"],\"options\":{\"variants\":[{\"src\":[\"./src/assets/fonts/atkinson-regular.woff\"],\"weight\":400,\"style\":\"normal\",\"display\":\"swap\"},{\"src\":[\"./src/assets/fonts/atkinson-bold.woff\"],\"weight\":700,\"style\":\"normal\",\"display\":\"swap\"}]}}],\"experimental\":{\"advancedRouting\":false,\"clientPrerender\":false,\"contentIntellisense\":false,\"chromeDevtoolsWorkspace\":false,\"rustCompiler\":false,\"queuedRendering\":{\"enabled\":false}},\"legacy\":{\"collectionsBackwardsCompat\":false}}","astro-version","6.4.6","content-config-digest","8940785073e53cbe"]